# The virtualenv, the PyInstaller work directory and the built app/DMG. All
# three are regenerated by `packaging/XAnalyze.spec` and together weigh about
# 2.3 GB, which is not something to carry in history.
venv/
# The interpreter this project ran on before 3.14, kept on disk until the
# upgrade has been lived with for a while. Delete it when you are sure.
venv-py39-old/
build/
dist/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store

# The user's own settings and API keys live here. Never committed: the file
# holds an Anthropic key when the user typed one into Settings.
settings.json
.xanalyze/

# `.xanalyze-ignore` is NOT here, and that is a change made on evidence.
# It was grouped with the settings file above, and it holds no secret: it is
# a list of paths and phrases a project says are not about itself. Keeping it
# untracked meant this repository could not tell anyone that `simulations/`
# is a folder of deliberately broken demo pages - so auditing this checkout
# reported 141 of its 143 findings from fixtures, for every contributor, for
# ever. A project's statement about itself belongs in the project.

# Test-account credentials for the live e2e run. The file says of itself that
# it is ignored by git; it was not, and `git add -A` would have committed a
# working subscription login. Checked with `git check-ignore` on 2026-08-20.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
